        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(sessions): derive list channels from agent keys",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users asking `sessions_list` to show archived or gateway-less group/channel sessions could see the channel reported as `unknown` when the only available routing metadata was an agent-scoped session key such as `agent:main:slack:channel:...`.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe sessions list channel fallback now derives from the request-key portion of canonical agent session keys before reading the existing `<channel>:(group|channel):...` shape. This keeps explicit `channel`, delivery context, and `lastChannel` precedence unchanged, and matches the Gateway sibling behavior for the same session-key contract.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. I reviewed the changed helper, `sessions_list` caller path, Gateway sibling parsing, and focused regression test.\n\n## User Impact\n\n`sessions_list` results now keep useful channel labels for agent-scoped Slack, Discord, Telegram, and similar group/channel sessions even when older or lightweight rows do not carry separate channel metadata.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Claim proved: `sessions_list` derives `channel: \"slack\"` from an agent-scoped group/channel session key when the Gateway row lacks separate `channel`, `origin.provider`, `deliveryContext.channel`, and `lastChannel` metadata.\n- Current head: `af8e15a0922baf31b1bbce02a748e2bf937070c2`.\n- Commands / artifacts:\n  - `git diff --check upstream/main...HEAD`\n  - `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/tools/sessions-list-tool.test.ts`\n  - `python .agents\\skills\\autoreview\\scripts\\autoreview --mode branch --base upstream/main`\n  - Repo-local runtime transcript through the real `sessions_list` tool with a redacted Gateway `sessions.list` row:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"head\": \"af8e15a0922baf31b1bbce02a748e2bf937070c2\",\n  \"tool\": \"sessions_list\",\n  \"gatewayMethods\": [\n    \"sessions.list\"\n  ],\n  \"requester\": \"agent:main:main\",\n  \"input\": {\n    \"key\": \"agent:main:slack:channel:C123:thread:1710000000.000100\",\n    \"kind\": \"group\",\n    \"spawnedBy\": \"agent:main:main\",\n    \"separateMetadataPresent\": {\n      \"channel\": false,\n      \"originProvider\": false,\n      \"deliveryContextChannel\": false,\n      \"lastChannel\": false\n    }\n  },\n  \"output\": {\n    \"count\": 1,\n    \"key\": \"agent:main:slack:channel:C123:thread:1710000000.000100\",\n    \"kind\": \"group\",\n    \"channel\": \"slack\",\n    \"spawnedBy\": \"agent:main:main\",\n    \"sessionId\": \"sess-redacted\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n- Observed result: focused Vitest passed with 1 file / 9 tests; diff hygiene passed; autoreview reported no accepted/actionable findings; the runtime transcript shows the real `sessions_list` tool returning `channel: \"slack\"` from the agent-scoped key.",
